---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Monisankar Nath | Software Engineer"
  description="Hi, I'm Monisankar Nath. I'm a Software Engineer specializing in React Native, iOS, and high-performance web systems. Read about my journey and experience."
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="about section">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Home</a>

      <h1>About</h1>

      <div class="content">
        <p class="intro">
          I'm a software engineer focused on building systems that work reliably
          at scale. My work spans mobile apps, web platforms, and the
          infrastructure that connects them.
        </p>

        <h2>What I Build</h2>
        <p>
          Most of my recent work has been in React Native and iOS development,
          with a focus on performance-critical features like video streaming,
          offline-first architectures, and real-time synchronization.
        </p>
        <p>
          I enjoy problems where the solution requires understanding systems
          deeply — not just the code, but how it interacts with networks,
          devices, and user behavior.
        </p>

        <h2>How I Think</h2>
        <p>
          I believe good engineering is about making thoughtful trade-offs, not
          chasing perfection. I prefer shipping early, measuring outcomes, and
          iterating based on real-world feedback.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm biased toward simplicity. Complex systems fail in complex ways.
          When possible, I choose boring technology and straightforward
          solutions.
        </p>

        <h2>Open Source</h2>
        <p>
          I maintain <a
            href="https://github.com/moni-synt/expo-video-cache"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">expo-video-cache</a
          >, a library for HLS video caching in React Native. It's used in
          production apps serving millions of streams.
        </p>
        <p>
          I contribute to open source because I've benefited enormously from it.
          Good libraries save thousands of hours of duplicated effort across the
          industry.
        </p>

        <h2>Currently</h2>
        <p>
          I'm working on improving video streaming performance in mobile
          applications, specifically around adaptive bitrate streaming and
          intelligent caching strategies.
        </p>

        <div class="cta-section">
          <a
            href="/Monisankar-Nath-Software-Engineer.pdf"
            class="btn btn-ghost"
            download
          >
            Download Resume →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-12);
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    transition: color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .content {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .content h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .content p {
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .cta-section {
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
</style>
